      "text": "To solve the problem we need to simplify \\(\\sqrt[4]{2^7 \\cdot 3^3}\\). We start by expressing the fourth root under the form of a product:\n\n\\[\n\\sqrt[4]{2^7 \\cdot 3^3} = 2^{7/4} \\cdot 3^{3/4}\n\\]\n\nThis can be written as:\n\n\\[\n2^{7/4} = \\sqrt[4]{2^7} = \\sqrt[4]{128} \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 3^{3/4} = \\sqrt[4]{27}\n\\]\n\nCombining these, the expression becomes:\n\n\\[\n2^{7/4} \\cdot 3^{3/4} = \\sqrt[4]{128} \\cdot \\sqrt[4]{27} = \\sqrt[4]{(128 \\cdot 27)}\n\\]\n\nNext, we calculate \\(128 \\cdot 27\\):\n\n\\[\n128 \\cdot 27 = 128 \\cdot (30 - 3) = 128 \\cdot 30 - 128 \\cdot 3 = 3840 - 384 = 3456\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the simplified root is:\n\n\\[\n\\sqrt[4]{3456}\n\\]\n\nWe need the final answer in the form \\(a \\sqrt[4]{b}\\), so:\n\n\\[\na = 12, \\quad b = 3456\n\\]\n\nNow, we find \\(a + b\\):\n\n\\[\na + b = 12 + 3456 = 3468\n\\]\n\nThe final answer is:\n\n\\(\\boxed{3468}\\)",
