      "text": "The given expression is $\\sqrt[4]{2^7\\cdot3^3}$.\n\nWe can rewrite the expression as $\\sqrt[4]{2^4\\cdot2^3\\cdot3^3}$.\n\nUsing the property $\\sqrt[n]{ab}=\\sqrt[n]{a}\\sqrt[n]{b}$, we can separate the expression as:\n\n$\\sqrt[4]{2^4\\cdot2^3\\cdot3^3}=\\sqrt[4]{2^4}\\cdot\\sqrt[4]{2^3}\\cdot\\sqrt[4]{3^3}$.\n\nSimplifying further, we have:\n\n$\\sqrt[4]{2^4}\\cdot\\sqrt[4]{2^3}\\cdot\\sqrt[4]{3^3}=2\\cdot2^{\\frac{3}{4}}\\cdot3^{\\frac{3}{4}}=2\\cdot3^{\\frac{3}{4}}\\cdot2^{\\frac{3}{4}}$.\n\nCombining the like terms, we have:\n\n$2\\cdot3^{\\frac{3}{4}}\\cdot2^{\\frac{3}{4}}=\\boxed{2\\sqrt[4]{54}}$.\n\nTherefore, $a=2$ and $b=54$, so $a+b=2+54=\\boxed{56}$.The answer is: 56",
